["Bundle the offline exercise catalog","A user can browse and inspect the attributed RepDB catalog in airplane mode from the first launch.","None (can start immediately).",["Pin the official RepDB package and ship the catalog and all free-tier flat illustrations in the app, including both poses when provided. Keep visible attribution and avoid a standalone copy of the dataset in source control.","Keep existing catalog search, filters, exercise selection, instructions, IDs and detail navigation working without a live catalog fetch.","Ensure newly saved exercise snapshots can display their illustrations offline. Preserve the readable detail path for earlier snapshots.","Cover the path through existing router tests and native bundle verification. Check an installed app in airplane mode and record the asset size impact."],"M"],
["Create and reopen workout templates in SQLite","A user can save a complete fixed-weight workout template locally and reopen it after a restart through the existing editor and Templates screens.","None (can start immediately).",["Add versioned SQLite initialization and local template create, list and detail operations behind the existing asynchronous service boundary.","Keep the current app default until the cutover. Exercise the SQLite service through existing screens using test or development composition.","Start empty, save each complete template atomically, and preserve template and placement identities, order, targets and saved exercise details on reopen after database recreation.","Retain the draft on a failed save and allow a safe retry without duplicate creation. Use the agreed router seam and verify against real SQLite where available."],"L"],
["Edit and delete SQLite workout templates","A user can maintain and remove locally saved workout templates through the existing editor.",[2],["Support whole-template edits, including exercising existing rename and reorder paths, and deletion through the injected SQLite service.","Replace each whole template atomically, preserving surviving placement identities and creation order. An update to a deleted template cannot recreate it.","Preserve Save and Cancel behavior and retain drafts or details for retry on failure. Repeat deletion safely.","Run the existing router-level behavior tests through the SQLite composition and check durable edit and delete outcomes."],"L"],
["Switch the app to local onboarding and storage","OpenFit launches and provides the full template workflow in airplane mode on a single device.",[1,3],["Replace the production email and sign-out flow with first-launch required display name entry, a small local-storage and backup notice, and a personalized greeting on Templates. Let the user edit the display name in Settings without changing training data.","Select SQLite by default, launch without Supabase configuration or a network connection, and keep appearance controls. Start with empty local training data and skip migration of the disposable hosted data.","On a supported device in airplane mode, start from a fresh install, browse the bundled catalog including illustrations, create a template, force-close and reopen, then edit and delete it. Verify a saved template persists across an app update. Record completed checks and any outstanding physical-device evidence.","This is the template-parity gate for M2. #47 and #49 depend on it, and #48 follows #47."],"L"],
["Remove the retired Supabase app integration","The local app has a single training-data implementation and can build and run without Supabase configuration.",[4],["Remove unused app authentication and Supabase client code, dependencies and obsolete app-side tests. Preserve tests for shared behavior under the SQLite implementation.","Verify the installed app can launch and use Templates without Supabase configuration. Run TypeScript, Jest and iOS and Android export checks.","Repository-level backend tooling retirement is tracked separately."],"M"],
["Retire the repository’s Supabase tooling","Contributors can set up and verify the SQLite app using the documented local workflow.",[4],["Remove obsolete backend-only commands and tooling from the active contributor workflow and update design, setup and verification instructions for SQLite.","Preserve historical decision records and make the native offline audit instructions reproducible.","Verify that the documented checks run from a clean checkout. Hosted project deletion is a separate maintainer action."],"M"]];
